From 56138eeacadd0c5ee5a192719cdf3baaa308de79 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chromium Extend <noreply@localhost>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 20:21:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 39/49] Use the Bare icon

Replaces the launcher icon in every density, plus the monochrome variant used by themed
launchers.

Three assets per density and each is framed differently, matching how upstream ships them:
app_icon is the legacy square icon at full bleed; layered_app_icon is the adaptive
foreground, inset so it sits inside the launcher mask over the white background declared in
ic_launcher.xml; layered_app_icon_background is the round icon, framed on the core of the
mark so it reads as a blue circle.

The framing matters more than it looks. A launcher shows roughly the central two thirds of
an adaptive icon and treats the rest as bleed, so art sized to cover the corners falls
outside the mask and only its middle survives.
